completeness. Material reversals require an explicit superseding decision rather
than a silent rewrite.

## Current repository scope

The repository currently contains architecture and repository documentation. It
does not yet contain:

- a Meridian Python package;
- runtime APIs;
- an adapter registry;
- evidence-inventory models;
- catalog discovery or canonical verification code;
- producer adapters;
- database schemas;
- grading-policy schemas;
- calculation engines;
- report schemas;
- subscriptions;
- delivery integrations; or
- production-ready functionality.

## Out of scope

Meridian does not own:

- raw scan ingestion or OCR;
- producer-native record schemas;
- producer manifest schemas or canonical validation;
- canonical Core registry writes;
- Core's Academic Period model;
- Core's publication registry or disposable catalog;
- arbitrary modification of producer records;
- roster or institution-wide person authority;
- intervention case management; or
- arbitrary-file parsing that guesses producer semantics.

Meridian does own consumer-side orchestration and producer adapters that call
producer-owned public contracts. This is distinct from owning or duplicating the
producer parser.

